<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Bruce Lee is seen at the epilepsy clinic by Dr. Abernathy-Leung eight days after the collapse, with the MRI done this morning and a sleep-deprived EEG this afternoon; he slept about four hours last night, as asked, for the EEG. He has had no further events. A colleague who was with him at the studio confirmed the account by telephone at his request: he came back from the restroom pale and sweating, said he felt faint, sank to the floor, became stiff with his arms flexed and then jerked all four limbs for about a minute with his eyes open, vomited, and was confused and unable to answer questions for about 20 minutes. Nobody saw how the event began. He remembers feeling hot, light-headed and nauseated in the restroom and nothing after that. He had slept about four hours a night for a week, had eaten little that day, had been drinking a lot of water in the hot booth, and had used cannabis that morning. He has never had a seizure, febrile seizures as a child, a serious head injury with loss of consciousness, meningitis, staring spells or jerks on waking, and no relative is known to have epilepsy. The emergency department sodium was 136 mmol/L and glucose 104 mg/dL, and the CT of the head was normal. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Witness account</td><td>Faint and hot, then stiffening and about a minute of jerking of all limbs, vomiting, 20 minutes of confusion; onset not seen</td></tr><tr><td>Triggers</td><td>A week of short sleep, missed meals, heat, large water intake, cannabis that morning</td></tr><tr><td>Emergency values</td><td>Sodium 136, glucose 104; CT head normal</td></tr><tr><td>MRI</td><td>Normal with an epilepsy protocol</td></tr><tr><td>EEG</td><td>Sleep-deprived EEG normal</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

